# Git hygiene

- Work on a feature branch; never commit directly to `master`.
- Pull latest `master` (and rebase) before starting work.
- Reference the GitHub issue in the commit body or PR — `Fixes #NNN` or `Refs #NNN`.
- Never commit commented-out code, debug prints/logging, `TODO(remove)` markers, or breakpoints.
- Never commit credentials, tokens, or `.env` files.
- Write a concise imperative commit subject (≤ 70 chars). Body explains WHY, not WHAT.
